Hashing templates toolbox 🛠️

 🔥 1. HashSet Template (for checking duplicates)

Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();

for (int num : nums) {
    if (set.contains(num)) {
        // Duplicate found
        return true;
    }
    set.add(num);
}
// No duplicates
return false;


✅ Used in:  
- Contains Duplicate
- Two Sum
- Checking for visited elements

---

 🔥 2. HashMap Template (for counting frequencies)

Map<Character, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();

for (char c : str.toCharArray()) {
    map.put(c, map.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);
}


✅ Used in:  
- Anagram Problems
- Character Frequency
- Majority Element

(Notice getOrDefault(c, 0) — very handy to avoid null errors!)

---

 🔥 3. Two Sum Trick (HashSet or HashMap)


Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
for (int num : nums) {
    if (set.contains(target - num)) {
        return true; // Found the pair
    }
    set.add(num);
}
return false;


✅ Used in:  
- Two Sum
- Pair Sum problems

(Save the complement while iterating — super smart!)

